      "id": 1,
      "text": "Samuel Fithian, an English settler, erected Fairton's first mill on Forke Creek before 1702.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairton%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Long before European arrival, the Lenape and Nanticoke peoples called the Fairton area home, speaking Algonquian languages.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairton%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Around 1763, the original mill dam was relocated near Clarks Pond Road, reshaping Fairton's early water power.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairton%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Between 1850 and 1897, Fairton's shipyards built three sloops, marking a brief but notable boatbuilding era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairton%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Nanticoke Lenni‑Lenape Tribal Nation’s cultural center sits in Fairton, while its tribal headquarters remain in nearby Bridgeton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairton%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In the 1810s, Fairton's economy pivoted to pork and beef, becoming the area's principal industry.",
